  "body": "## What changed\n\nA finishing operation can now post for an eligible model opened at reduced accuracy. The model page and program header state the true-surface bound.\n\nThe importer records whether the file tolerance caused the coarse mesh. Import, project save/load, model copies, stock copies and undo preserve this record. Update undo restores each copy's own cause. A cause change invalidates cached verdicts. Missing records, budget coarsening and mixed causes keep the strict law of #864.\n\nFor an eligible model, the chord `c` selects the law:\n\n| Chord | Mesh allowance |\n|---|---|\n| Up to 0.010 mm | The existing strict law. |\n| Over 0.010 mm through 0.020 mm | `min(t - 0.005, 0.005)` mm, where `t` is the law's tolerance. |\n| Over 0.020 mm | The existing strict law. No allowance remains at `DEV_TOL`; the operation is refused by name. |\n\nThe allowance never exceeds the law's tolerance. Collision bands still grow by the full excess. Turning, rotary and probe guards keep their strict laws. The program gate also keeps the strict law for those operation kinds.\n\nAt a chord of 0.019 mm, the mesh allowance is 0.005 mm. The true-surface bound is 0.024 mm. The header says:\n\n```text\nReduced accuracy: model brick was checked to 0.024 mm, not 0.010 mm\n```\n\nThe model page and MCP facts state the same bound. The display rounds the bound upward. A chord of 0.0192 mm gives a numerical bound of 0.0242 mm and a displayed bound of 0.025 mm.\n\nThe engine sends each header note through `onComment` after `onOpen`. All 19 shipped posts use valid dialect comments and preserve the complete bound. A custom post can omit the note.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2996-wide-verdict.md`. The maximum widened true-surface bound is 0.025 mm. This is below the maintainer's accepted 0.030 mm limit.\n\n## UI evidence\n\nThe model page now states both the mesh approximation and the true-surface bound used by the checks. The UI import path also preserves the recorded cause during a model update.\n\nBoth images render the actual Properties page through the existing egui shell test harness, with the same model at a 0.019 mm chord. The after image uses the current head. The before image uses the summary function body from `upstream/main`, temporarily substituted into the same harness. The harness uses a placeholder viewport. All temporary source edits were restored.\n\nThe temporary UI assertion `pr_3087_reduced_accuracy_note_capture` passed on this head. Substituting the old summary made it fail. Restoring this head made it pass again.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Model note before this change](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/63c577851d096674d43364f7e6722c04b75d3430/3087/model-note-before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![Model note after this change](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/63c577851d096674d43364f7e6722c04b75d3430/3087/model-note-after.png)\n\nThe images are stored only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch. No image, log or review evidence is committed to this PR branch.\n\n## Tests and mutation checks\n\nThe main pins are:\n\n- `comment_escape::header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound`: all 19 shipped posts, with hostile note text.\n- `model_excess::absent_or_budget_cause_keeps_the_original_mesh_tolerance`: missing and budget causes keep the original boundary assertions.\n- `model_fidelity_cause`: import, persistence, copies and undo preserve the cause.\n- `model_fidelity_wide`: a permitted model posts with the header note; a model beyond the limit is refused; a deeper gouge blocks posting. The suite also checks upward rounding and cache invalidation after a cause change.\n- `model_excess::an_eligible_file_caps_larger_law_tolerances_at_the_header_allowance` and `coarse_probe_plasma::a_file_tolerance_plasma_check_keeps_the_stated_true_surface_bound`: larger base tolerances also respect the 0.005 mm cap.\n- `coarse_laws`: rotary operations keep the strict law.\n\nThe [author's follow-up](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/3087#issuecomment-7058458064) records 39 focused tests passed. All 12 mutations failed with the relevant fix removed, then passed after restoration.\n\nThe [latest independent review](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/3087#issuecomment-7059566865) repeated two mutations. Taking the full excess failed at `model_excess.rs:312`. Using the widened deduction for collision-band growth failed at line 317. After restoration, all 16 tests in `model_excess` and `coarse_collision` passed.\n\nNo fixture, golden or snapshot PNG changes belong to this PR.\n\n## Gate evidence\n\nValidated head: `fb3e8cf4c8627ee9f3408b81340515df3d6fa70a`.\n\nThe latest independent review used `upstream/main` at `11402dba4c849c5f827dccebc14f850196614311`. Its trial merge was clean. All checks ran locally.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All 1,021 steps passed. The geometry change selects the batch plan. The logs total 9,196 passed tests, 87 ignored and zero failed. Builds and clippy with `--all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: GREEN. Both steps passed, including the release light test.\n- Explicit extra suites: kernel `step_agreement`, 26 passed; kernel `machining_mesh`, seven passed; app `feature_edge_g1_join`, five passed.\n\nA fresh author-side run on this unchanged head completed all 1,021 quick-gate steps: RED, 40 failed steps. Clippy passed with `--all-targets -- -D warnings` across geometry, CL, tools, post, sim, motion, app and UI.\n\nThe shared build directory made the affected app and UI tests resolve post and machine assets from the main checkout. All 38 affected app suites passed when their test executables ran from a worktree-local directory with this branch's assets: 584 tests passed, zero failed. The two affected UI tests also passed with the correct assets. The complete UI library rerun passed: 1,378 passed, zero failed and seven ignored.\n\nThe remaining `vertical_arc_entry` assertions are `each level still descends on a chord fan` and the stale `vertical_arc_x.cl` path assertion. Earlier author and review comments record these assertions failing on their clean main baseline. No source change was made for these out-of-scope failures. The complete fresh gate remains RED; the isolated reruns do not change that result.\n\n### Heavy lanes\n\nThe author's run on this exact head completed `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All 236 steps completed. There were 100 passed tests and six registered known failures under #1950 and #2849. The known failures failed as expected and were not counted as passes.\n\nThe reached lanes were:\n\n- Kernel heavy: `step_agreement` passed.\n- Motion heavy: all reached targets passed, including the registered known-failure checks.\n- App heavy: all reached targets passed, including the registered known-failure checks.\n\nThe corrected `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` test passed. All six `rotary_field_parity` tests and all six `shared_face_bodies_finish` tests passed. The latest review independently ran the light lane and accepted this heavy evidence for the unchanged head.\n\n## Limits\n\nThe widened checks can miss a true-surface gouge up to `c + 0.005` mm. The header states this bound. Models coarsened by the facet budget retain the original protection. Turning, rotary and probe operations do not receive this wider permission.\n\nChangelog: Eligible models made coarse by the file tolerance can post with chord errors through 0.020 mm. The model page and program header state the true-surface bound. Budget models and collision bands keep their existing safety laws.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation).\n\nFixes #2996\n",
